---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/Colophon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { getPublishedPosts } from '../lib/writing';

const showWriting = (await getPublishedPosts()).length > 0;
const access = site.links.edgarMiner ?? `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Edgar Miner access')}`;
const accessText = site.links.edgarMiner ? 'try it' : 'ask for access';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.description}>
  <Nav slot="nav" showWriting={showWriting} />
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>{site.headline}</h1>
    <p class="purpose">Point-in-time financials. Company relationships traced to the source.</p>

    <p>See a company's financials as they were publicly available on a given date, without later restatements slipping into the picture. Explore a relationship graph of who supplies whom and who owns what, with every connection linked to its source.</p>

    <p>Built on SEC filings. Available through API, chat, and MCP.</p>

    <p>I'm Chandni, an engineer and the founder of <a href="/work/edgar-miner/">Edgar Miner</a>. If you research companies for a living, <a href={access}>{accessText}</a>.</p>

    {site.hero && <Media items={[site.hero]} />}

    <p>Before Edgar Miner, I built <a href="/work/talewriter/">Talewriter</a>. It started one evening when I couldn't convince my then three-year-old to eat her vegetables.</p>

    <p>I made her an AI storybook where she was the heroine of a veggie world. To my surprise, she ate the vegetables. I started making books for friends and family, weaving their children's cultures and everyday lives into the stories.</p>

    <p>I built Talewriter myself and ran a pilot that put 50+ personalized books into a Manhattan preschool. More than 90% of parents and teachers asked for more.</p>

    <p>Before that, I built backend systems. I shipped a Chrome extension at Slice that <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2016/08/23/slices-new-browser-add-on-will-email-you-when-prices-drop/">TechCrunch</a> and <a href="https://lifehacker.com/slice-watch-for-chrome-will-send-you-price-alert-emails-1785669278">Lifehacker</a> wrote about. At Rakuten, I led backend development for <a href="https://www.rakuten.com/dining">Rakuten Dining</a>, a rewards product with 10,000+ restaurants, and helped teams adopt serverless architecture, reducing infrastructure costs by 80%. At <a href="https://www.serverless.com/">Serverless</a>, I rebuilt billing on Stripe and cut processing time by 98%.</p>

    <p>Talewriter taught me how much of running a company happens outside the code. That took me to NYU Stern for a <a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/programs-admissions/tech-mba">Tech MBA</a>, where I studied entrepreneurship and strategy and worked with deep-tech founders at <a href="https://endlessfrontierlabs.com/">Endless Frontier Labs</a> on product, go-to-market, and fundraising.</p>

    <p>Seeing how much time founders spent on investor outreach led me to build <a href="/work/fundraising-agent/">Fundraising Agent</a>, which automates the work of running an outreach campaign.</p>

    <p class="lines">Some things have worked. Others haven't made it very far. Entrepreneurs aren't defined by their first 87 ideas. {site.links.ideas && <a href={site.links.ideas}>Here's the list.</a>}</p>

    <p>I speak five languages, too. Happy to start there.</p>

    <p class="ps">If any of this overlaps with what you're working on, I'd love to hear from you. <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <Colophon slot="colophon" />
</Base>
